From 4a39e4c70e1d8f2a2c0f1a1e0c0a4a39e4c70e1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 12:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: coda: use linear GDI map for Coda980 NV12 input

coda_s_fmt() programs the GDI source fetcher for the tiled frame
MB-raster map when NV12 is selected on a CODA_960 BIT device. On i.MX6
that is correct: the tiled map pairs with the VDOA detiler, which also
produces tiled NV12 frames.

The SG2002 Coda980 reports CODA_960 as its product code, so it inherits
that branch, but it has no tiled-source producer: userspace hands over
plain linear-raster NV12 buffers. The encoder then fetches the linear
buffer through the MB-raster tile walker. The programmed source
addresses and the DRAM contents behind them are both correct (verified
by /dev/mem dump of the source buffer after a corrupt encode), yet the
decoded frame shows fine vertical stripes with the right mean luma and
destroyed chroma: the fetch order, not the data, is scrambled. Direct
NV12 input measured 12.6 dB PSNR against the source frame where the
staged NV21 control measures 43.2 dB.

Keep NV12 on GDI_LINEAR_FRAME_MAP for devices with the Coda980 H.264
ABI, the same map NV21 and the planar formats already use. With the
linear map, direct NV12 input encodes cleanly on SG2002: 43.2 dB PSNR
over 60 frames at 640x480 against the source frame, matching the staged
NV21 control bit for bit.

Signed-off-by: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-common.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-common.c b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-common.c
index 6f4f49dd0..4a39e4c70 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-common.c
@@ -894,7 +894,8 @@ static int coda_s_fmt(struct coda_ctx *ctx, struct v4l2_format *f,
 		break;
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12:
 		if (!disable_tiling && ctx->use_bit &&
-		    ctx->dev->devtype->product == CODA_960) {
+		    ctx->dev->devtype->product == CODA_960 &&
+		    !ctx->dev->devtype->has_coda980_h264_abi) {
 			ctx->tiled_map_type = GDI_TILED_FRAME_MB_RASTER_MAP;
 			break;
 		}
